nils-lst-ai: the third-party components in this image and their terms

Beside NILS's own files (AGPL-3.0-only, https://github.com/kineuro/nils), this
image is LST-AI's own image, jqmcginnis/lst-ai v1.2.0 by LST-AI's authors,
pinned by its manifest digest in Dockerfile, with one thin layer on top. The
layer does four things: it removes the image's ENTRYPOINT, it puts HD-BET's
parameters in /opt/hd-bet_params where every account reads them, it changes one
line of HD-BET's paths.py to name that folder, and it adds this notice and the
licence texts beside it, in /usr/local/share/licenses/nils-lst-ai. LST-AI's
code, weights and atlas, greedy, the rest of HD-BET's code and every library
are the upstream image's, byte for byte.

Research use only. LST-AI's authors say: "LST-AI is a research-only tool for MS
Lesion Segmentation and has not been validated, licensed or approved for any
clinical usage." It is no medical device, and nothing here changes that.

