greedy (https://github.com/pyushkevich/greedy), the registration LST-AI calls:
Paul Yushkevich, University of Pennsylvania. The greedy in /usr/local/bin is
built from the source commit of 18 May 2023 that LST-AI's image names, and that
source is under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later
(greedy-COPYING.txt beside this file, and the headers of its source files). Its
source is in this image, in /greedy, as the licence asks of whoever passes the
program on. The project moved to the Apache License 2.0 in August 2026, after
this build, and this build keeps its own terms. It is built with ITK 5.2.1
(Apache-2.0) and VTK 9.1.0 (BSD-3-Clause), linked into it. The package's
binaries folder holds another build of greedy, of October 2023, which lst does
not call: it runs the greedy on the search path.

The Apache License 2.0 (TensorFlow 2.13.1, Keras 2.13.1, SimpleITK 2.4.0 and
others among the Python packages) is HD-BET-LICENSE.txt beside this file. Other
Python packages (PyTorch 2.1.0, NumPy, SciPy, scikit-image, nibabel) are under
their own licences. Every Python package carries its licence in its dist-info
folder, and every Ubuntu 22.04 package in /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright.

